# Batch files MUST keep CRLF line endings.
#
# cmd.exe resolves "call :label" by BYTE OFFSET into the script. With
# LF-only endings the offset arithmetic drifts, and cmd silently
# re-executes parts of the file (observed: stages 7/8/9 ran 7 times in
# a single invocation while stages 1-6 ran once). The symptom looks like
# a logic bug in the script, not a line-ending problem, so it is very
# easy to misdiagnose.
#
# "eol=crlf" makes git check them out with CRLF even if a tool rewrote
# them with LF (which is exactly what happened here).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell / source files stay LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
